<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottawa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ottawa is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, on the Ottawa river in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>. Founded as Bytown in 1826 during the building of the Rideau Canal, it was renamed in 1855 and chosen by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a> in 1857 as capital of the Province of Canada, a choice confirmed at Confederation in 1867. The name is often used for the Canadian federal government itself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottawa.jpg" alt="Ottawa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Arctic.gnome assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parliament-Ottawa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
